# 16: dual-emulator-safe 2P match — P1 Demitri (default cursor) vs P2 two
# cursor-rights (Victor), NO in-match inputs (pure neutral after the picks).
#
# Authored for cross-emulator field comparison (CLAUDE.md §4): MAME and FBNeo
# run the same states a few frames apart, so menu presses near a screen
# transition can land on opposite sides of an input-accept boundary and
# change WHICH content runs (docs/GOTCHAS.md: 03's S2 at +30 after S1 joins
# P2 on MAME but not on FBNeo). Rules used here:
#   - system/menu presses at least 100 frames after the enabling transition
#   - no press within ~±10 frames of any expected transition
#   - cursor moves stay short (3 frames — no autorepeat ambiguity) but are
#     placed on a long-stable screen
#   - nothing after the picks, so every post-anchor frame is input-neutral
300-305 sys=C1
420-425 sys=C2
800-803 sys=S1
940-943 sys=S2
# both on select screen, stable
1100-1102 p2=R
1160-1162 p2=R
1300-1302 p1=1
1360-1362 p2=1
# speed menus time out on their own; match starts ~2500-2900; run long past
# the anchor + comparator windows
4200 wait
